  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The masses of Planet A and Planet B are 3<em>M</em> and 4<em>M</em> respectively. The radius of Planet A is 36<em>R</em> and the radius of Planet B is 6<em>R</em>. A satellite orbits Planet B at a distance of 2<em>R</em> above the surface of the planet. The speed of the satellite is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v_B\"></span>. The escape speed from Planet A is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v_A\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is the ratio <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{v_A}{v_B}\"></span> ?</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\">3</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{3}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{3}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
